IMPORT prelude

-- Stamp Duties (Spouses) (Remission of ABSD) Rules 2013 (S 217/2013), made under s 74 of the Stamp Duties Act 1929 -- remission
-- of additional buyer's stamp duty (ABSD) where a married couple buy one residential property together.
--
-- Edition: the version current at 10 October 2026 (amendments to S 245/2023 wef 27 April 2023), saved by hand from SSO and
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SDA1929-S217-2013.txt.
--
-- WHY. Added on 11 October 2026 for REQ-0009 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl (cradle-to-grave-simone, event e081, on the
-- alternative ordering where the couple buy before they sell): on what conditions, and within what time, is ABSD remitted?
--
-- DATES are calendar dates (year, month, day), because rule 4(3)(c) counts months. "Within 6 months after" a date is read as
-- ON OR BEFORE the same day of the month six months later; where that month is shorter, its last day. That reading is the
-- encoder's, not the Rules'.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: who counts as owning property beyond the inputs (rule 2(5) to (6): partnership and trust property, land under
-- acquisition, s 22C settlors are disregarded or treated specially -- the caller decides the count); the Commissioner's
-- discretion to allow a longer refund period (an input); trust arrangements before 9 May 2022.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Stamp Duties (Spouses) (Remission of ABSD) Rules 2013`

§§ `Dates`

DECLARE Date HAS
    year IS A NUMBER
    month IS A NUMBER
    day IS A NUMBER

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
    ((y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0) AND (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))) OR (y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0)

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` y m MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` y THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF m EQUALS 4 OR m EQUALS 6 OR m EQUALS 9 OR m EQUALS 11 THEN 30 ELSE 31

-- A single number that orders dates: later dates give larger numbers.
GIVEN d IS A Date
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ordinal of` d MEANS d's year TIMES 10000 PLUS d's month TIMES 100 PLUS d's day

GIVEN a IS A Date, b IS A Date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls on or before` a b IF `the ordinal of` a AT MOST `the ordinal of` b

GIVEN d IS A Date, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Date
`the date months after` d n MEANS
    Date WITH year IS `the new year`, month IS `the new month`, day IS `the new day`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS d's year TIMES 12 PLUS d's month MINUS 1 PLUS n
        `the new year` MEANS FLOOR (`the month count` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month` MEANS `the month count` MINUS `the new year` TIMES 12 PLUS 1
        `the new day` MEANS
            IF d's day GREATER THAN `the number of days in month` `the new year` `the new month`
            THEN `the number of days in month` `the new year` `the new month`
            ELSE d's day

§§ `Rule 2 -- definitions`

-- Rule 2(1): "Singapore citizen not owning property", "... owning one property", and the same for permanent residents and
-- foreigners: whether the person, "if not for the transaction which is the subject of the exempt instrument", beneficially
-- owns an estate or interest in no residential property, or in one, in Singapore.
DECLARE Residence IS ONE OF
    `Singapore citizen`
    `Singapore permanent resident`
    foreigner

DECLARE Spouse HAS
    residence IS A Residence
    `residential properties owned apart from this purchase` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN s IS A Spouse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a citizen not owning property` s IF
    s's residence EQUALS `Singapore citizen` AND s's `residential properties owned apart from this purchase` EQUALS 0

GIVEN s IS A Spouse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a citizen owning one property` s IF
    s's residence EQUALS `Singapore citizen` AND s's `residential properties owned apart from this purchase` EQUALS 1

GIVEN s IS A Spouse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a non-citizen not owning property` s IF
    (NOT (s's residence EQUALS `Singapore citizen`)) AND s's `residential properties owned apart from this purchase` EQUALS 0

GIVEN s IS A Spouse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is anyone owning one property` s IF
    s's `residential properties owned apart from this purchase` EQUALS 1

GIVEN s IS A Spouse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a non-citizen owning at most one property` s IF
    (NOT (s's residence EQUALS `Singapore citizen`)) AND s's `residential properties owned apart from this purchase` AT MOST 1

-- The facts at the time the instrument is executed (rules 3(1), 4(1)).
DECLARE Purchase HAS
    `number of joint parties` IS A NUMBER
    `the parties are married to each other` IS A BOOLEAN
    `first party` IS A Spouse
    `second party` IS A Spouse
    `to be held as partnership property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `executed on or after 9 May 2022 and to be held on trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `executed on` IS A Date

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a married couple buying together` p IF
    p's `number of joint parties` EQUALS 2 AND p's `the parties are married to each other`

§§ `Rule 3 -- spouses neither of whom owns property`

-- Rule 3(1): the full ABSD is remitted on a purchase of a single residential property where there are "2 (and only 2) joint
-- parties", "married to each other", and they are "respectively, a Singapore citizen not owning property and either a
-- Singapore permanent resident not owning property or a foreigner not owning property". (2): not for partnership property.
-- (3): not where, for an instrument executed on or after 9 May 2022, either party holds on trust.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `rule 3 remits the ABSD` p IF
        `is a married couple buying together` p
    AND (    (`is a citizen not owning property` (p's `first party`) AND `is a non-citizen not owning property` (p's `second party`))
          OR (`is a citizen not owning property` (p's `second party`) AND `is a non-citizen not owning property` (p's `first party`)))
    AND NOT p's `to be held as partnership property`
    AND NOT p's `executed on or after 9 May 2022 and to be held on trust`

§§ `Rule 4 -- spouses one or both of whom owns one property`

-- Rule 4(2): one of three descriptions --
--   (a) one is a citizen not owning property, the other owns one property (citizen, PR or foreigner);
--   (b) one is a citizen owning one property, the other is a PR or foreigner owning none or one;
--   (c) each is a citizen owning one property, "whether or not it is the same residential property".
GIVEN x IS A Spouse, y IS A Spouse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fit description (a) or (b) in that order` x y IF
       (`is a citizen not owning property` x AND `is anyone owning one property` y)
    OR (`is a citizen owning one property` x AND `is a non-citizen owning at most one property` y)

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fit a rule 4(2) description` p IF
       `fit description (a) or (b) in that order` (p's `first party`) (p's `second party`)
    OR `fit description (a) or (b) in that order` (p's `second party`) (p's `first party`)
    OR (`is a citizen owning one property` (p's `first party`) AND `is a citizen owning one property` (p's `second party`))

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is within rule 4(1)` p IF
    `is a married couple buying together` p AND `fit a rule 4(2) description` p

-- What happens after the purchase, for the conditions in rule 4(3).
DECLARE Aftermath HAS
    `ABSD paid to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `TOP or CSC granted on or before the date of execution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earlier of TOP and CSC` IS A Date
    `every property that made a party an owner has been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of the last disposal` IS A Date
    `either party acquired another residential property before that disposal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on that date the two own the new property together and with no one else` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on that date they remain married` IS A BOOLEAN
    `refund claimed on` IS A Date
    `the Commissioner allowed a longer period for the claim` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Rule 4(3)(c): the clock runs from execution, or, "if no TOP or CSC is granted or issued ... on the date of execution", from
-- the grant or issue of "the TOP or of the CSC, whichever is the earlier".
GIVEN p IS A Purchase, a IS A Aftermath
GIVETH A Date
`the date the disposal clock starts` p a MEANS
    IF a's `TOP or CSC granted on or before the date of execution` THEN p's `executed on` ELSE a's `earlier of TOP and CSC`

-- Rule 4(3A): if the instrument was executed on or before 1 June 2020 and the six-month deadline falls on or after
-- 1 February 2020, the period is 12 months.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase, a IS A Aftermath
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the disposal period in months` p a MEANS
    IF     `falls on or before` (p's `executed on`) (Date WITH year IS 2020, month IS 6, day IS 1)
       AND `falls on or before` (Date WITH year IS 2020, month IS 2, day IS 1) (`the date months after` (`the date the disposal clock starts` p a) 6)
    THEN 12
    ELSE 6

GIVEN p IS A Purchase, a IS A Aftermath
GIVETH A Date
`the last day to dispose of the other property` p a MEANS
    `the date months after` (`the date the disposal clock starts` p a) (`the disposal period in months` p a)

-- Rule 4(3)(f): the refund claim is made within 6 months after the date of disposal "or such longer period as the
-- Commissioner may allow in a particular case". (4): where two properties were disposed of on different dates, the later date.
GIVEN a IS A Aftermath
GIVETH A Date
`the last day to claim the refund` a MEANS `the date months after` (a's `date of the last disposal`) 6

GIVEN p IS A Purchase, a IS A Aftermath
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rule 4(3) conditions are met` p a IF
        NOT p's `to be held as partnership property`                                                       -- (a)
    AND NOT p's `executed on or after 9 May 2022 and to be held on trust`                                   -- (aa)
    AND a's `ABSD paid to the Commissioner`                                                                -- (b)
    AND a's `every property that made a party an owner has been disposed of`                               -- (c)
    AND `falls on or before` (a's `date of the last disposal`) (`the last day to dispose of the other property` p a)
    AND NOT a's `either party acquired another residential property before that disposal`                  -- (d)
    AND a's `on that date the two own the new property together and with no one else`                      -- (e)(i)
    AND a's `on that date they remain married`                                                             -- (e)(ii)
    AND (    `falls on or before` (a's `refund claimed on`) (`the last day to claim the refund` a)          -- (f)
          OR a's `the Commissioner allowed a longer period for the claim`)

GIVEN p IS A Purchase, a IS A Aftermath
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `rule 4 remits the ABSD` p a IF
    `is within rule 4(1)` p AND `the rule 4(3) conditions are met` p a

§§ `Result`

-- Rule 3 remits at the outset; rule 4 only by refund of ABSD already paid (condition (b)).
GIVEN p IS A Purchase, a IS A Aftermath, `ABSD chargeable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ABSD remitted` p a `ABSD chargeable` MEANS
    IF `rule 3 remits the ABSD` p OR `rule 4 remits the ABSD` p a THEN `ABSD chargeable` ELSE 0
